# Line endings are decided here, not by each machine's `core.autocrlf`.
#
# Git for Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true` system-wide, which checks files
# out as CRLF and converts them back to LF on commit. Every text file in this
# repo is already LF in the index, so that round-trip changed nothing and only
# produced the "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings on `git add` — noise on
# every release commit. `eol=lf` keeps the working copy matching the index, so
# the conversion (and the warning) never happens.
#
# This also keeps Linux CI and the Dockerfile.vercel build byte-identical to a
# Windows checkout, which matters for anything that hashes or diffs a file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never inspected for line endings, never diffed as text. `text=auto`
# already detects most of these, but stating it removes the guesswork for
# formats whose headers can look textual.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.ico   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.pdf   binary
